# DECISION RULES

- **include**: the abstract clearly meets all inclusion criteria.
- **exclude**: the abstract clearly violates at least one inclusion criterion or matches an explicit exclusion criterion.
- **uncertain**: cannot decide from the abstract alone, so full-text review is needed. Use this rather than guessing.

# TASK

Record your verdict for the abstract in the user message. Judge it against the criteria above and nothing else.

- Base every judgement on what the abstract actually says. Do not infer from the title or the journal.
- When you cite a criterion, use the criterion IDs exactly as they appear above.
- Keep the reasoning to one or two sentences, and quote the abstract verbatim when you quote it.
- Be strict. When in doubt, prefer "uncertain" over guessing.

You will also be asked to re-check each criterion separately: one verdict (PASS / FAIL / UNCERTAIN) per criterion, with a one-sentence reason, a confidence from 1 to 10, and a supporting quote.

